{
  "claim": "phi = 2(pi - x_a)(pi - x_b) = 2 pi^2 - 2 pi (x_a + x_b) + 2 x_a x_b; the 'nearly constant' explanation was wrong",
  "implemented_unitary": "U(x) = [ D(x) H^{(x)n} ]^reps,  D(x) = exp(-i [ sum_q u_q Z_q + sum_(a,b) (pi - u_a)(pi - u_b) Z_a Z_b ]),  u = bandwidth * x, linear chain pairs (q, q+1), reps = 2 (src/quantum/simulator.py ZZFeatureMap.states)",
  "gate_identity_CNOT_RZ2phi_CNOT_equals_exp_minus_i_phi_ZZ": true,
  "matches_qiskit_ZZFeatureMap_gate_sequence": "yes, apart from entanglement: Qiskit's default is 'full', V9 uses 'linear'",
  "periodicity": "exp(-i phi Z_a Z_b) changes only by a global phase when phi -> phi + pi, and exp(-i u Z) when u -> u + pi; so the constant pi^2 acts as a fixed ZZ rotation with phi = pi^2 mod pi = 0.4448 rad",
  "note_on_linear_terms": "all three parts (constant, linear, bilinear) multiply Z_a Z_b, so all three are two-qubit interactions; the linear part is an entangling ZZ rotation whose angle depends additively on the data, only the bilinear part couples the two features multiplicatively",
